index 00000000..fab001a4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/lib/networks/booking/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@
+<!--
+SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Janis Blechert <janis@blechert.at>
+SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
+-->
+
+# Ticket shop deep links
+
+`ticket-shops.json` describes ticket shops for which KPublicTransport can generate
+a link that opens the shop with origin, destination and departure date/time already
+filled in. Those links are returned by `JourneySection::bookingUrl` and
+`Journey::bookingUrl` when the backend did not provide a booking link itself.
+
+The file is part of the online updatable data, so entries that use features an
+older version of the library does not support are dropped individually (with a
+warning) rather than invalidating the entire file.
+
+## Schema
+
+The top level is `{ "shops": [ ... ] }`, sorted by `id`. If several shops match,
+explicit operator matches win over generic matches, and file order breaks ties.
+If a shop cannot generate a link (e.g. a required station identifier is missing)
+the next matching shop is tried.
+
+Each shop has the following properties:
+
+- `id` (required): `<ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code or "eu">_<name>`, lower case, unique.
+- `name` (required): human readable name, informational only.
+- `verified` (optional): date when the link format was last checked in a browser.
+- `notes` (optional): free text.
+- `match` (required): when to offer this shop for a journey section.
+  - `countries` (required): upper case ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes. Both ends of each
+    section have to be in one of those countries. The country of a location is taken from
+    `Location::country`, or if that is unknown from its UIC or IBNR station code.
+  - `requireCountries` (optional): at least one end of the section (or of the entire
+    journey) has to be in one of those countries.
+  - `departureCountries` (optional): the section (or the entire journey) has to start in one
+    of those countries. Useful to prefer the shop of the departure country for cross-border
+    journeys that several shops sell.
+  - `lineModes` (optional): `KPublicTransport::Line::Mode` key names, defaults to
+    `["LongDistanceTrain", "Train", "LocalTrain"]`.
+  - `operators` (optional): `{ "names": [...], "hosts": [...], "matchUnknown": false }`.
+    `names` are case-insensitive regular expressions matched against `Line::operatorName`,
+    `hosts` are matched against the host of `Line::operatorUrl` (including sub-domains,
+    ignoring a `www.` prefix). Without this, the shop matches any operator. With this,
+    sections with a different operator name do not match, and sections without an operator
+    name only match if `matchUnknown` is `true` (or if their operator URL matches). An
+    operator URL alone does not identify an operator, as some backends set their own URL
+    for all lines. Names have to cover the spellings used by the backends, e.g. localized
+    names used by the DB backend.
+  - `excludeOperators` (optional): `{ "names": [...], "hosts": [...] }`, operators that
+    are not sold by this shop.
+- `stationIdentifiers` (required when using `{from.id}` or `{to.id}`): ordered list of
+  `{ "type": "<Location identifier type>", "aliases": { ... }, "pattern": "<regexp>", "uicCountries": [...] }`.
+  The first entry for which the location has a non-empty identifier that matches the
+  (optional, anchor it yourself) pattern is used. If `uicCountries` is set, the identifier
+  must be a valid UIC/IBNR station code from one of those UIC countries, and its last
+  seven digits are used. `aliases` (optional) maps identifier values to the values the shop
+  uses, e.g. for pseudo stations a backend uses for parts of a station. It is applied before
+  checking `pattern` and `uicCountries`.
+- `languages` (required when using `{lang}`): ordered list of
+  `{ "code": "<language>", "value": "<inserted text, defaults to code>", "script": "<optional>" }`.
+  An entry with a `script` (`Greek`, `Cyrillic`, `Arabic`, `Hebrew`, `Georgian`, `Armenian`)
+  is used if the origin station name contains characters of that script. Otherwise the
+  first entry without `script` matching the user's UI languages is used, falling back to
+  the first entry without `script`.
+- `nameAliases` (optional): maps station names to the names the shop uses, for shops
+  that only accept their own station names.
+- `url` (required): `https://` URL template, see below.
+
+## URL templates
+
+Placeholders have the form `{name}`, `{name:format}` or `{name|filter|filter}`. Literal
+curly brackets have to be written as `%7B` and `%7D`.
+
+| Placeholder | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `{from.name}`, `{to.name}` | Station name. |
+| `{from.id}`, `{to.id}` | Station identifier, see `stationIdentifiers`. |
+| `{from.country}`, `{to.country}` | ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code (upper case). |
+| `{departure:FORMAT}` | Scheduled departure in local time of the origin, formatted with a `QDateTime::toString` format. |
+| `{arrival:FORMAT}` | Scheduled arrival in local time of the destination. |
+| `{departure.minutesOfDay}` | Minutes since midnight of the local departure time. |
+| `{lang}` | Language value, see `languages`. |
+
+Station placeholders support the following filters, applied in order before
+the value is percent-encoded:
+
+- `capture`: only for `{from.id}` and `{to.id}`, and only as the first filter: use the
+  first capturing group of the `pattern` of the station identifier rule that provided the
+  identifier, rather than the entire identifier. This allows to use parts of identifiers,
+  e.g. a national station code without the UIC country code. All station identifier rules
+  of the shop need a `pattern` with a capturing group then.
+- `json`: escape for use inside a JSON string.
+- `slug`: remove diacritics and replace whitespace with `-`.
+- `lower`: convert to lower case.
+- `plus`: encode spaces as `+` rather than `%20`.
+
+Date/time, minutes of day and language values are inserted verbatim. Quote literal
+characters in date/time formats (e.g. `'T'`), and write characters that need
+encoding in their encoded form (e.g. `HH'%3A'mm` for an encoded colon).
+
+If any placeholder has no value, the shop is skipped.
+
+## Adding a shop
+
+- Only add shops whose deep link format was verified, ideally in a browser, and set
+  `verified` accordingly.
+- Add at least one row to `testGolden` in `autotests/ticketshoptest.cpp` with a real
+  example URL. `testTable` fails for shops without such a row.
+- Shops that need operator-specific station codes (that is, codes KPublicTransport does
+  not have as location identifiers, nor as part of one) cannot be supported yet.
